## Docker Compose

The generated `docker-compose.yml` uses local placeholder credentials and
includes only the selected services:

- The application image when Docker or Compose is selected.
- PostgreSQL when PostgreSQL is selected, with database `app` and the
  credentials `postgres` / `postgres`.
- MySQL when MySQL/MariaDB is selected, with database `app` and the
  credentials `root` / `root`.
- RabbitMQ when RabbitMQ is selected, with the management UI on port `15672`.
- Redis when Redis is selected, with a persistent volume.
- An ARQ worker when ARQ is selected, built from the same image as the app.
- A Celery worker when Celery is selected, built from the same image as the app.

PostgreSQL, MySQL, RabbitMQ, and Redis include healthchecks. Start the stack with:

```sh
docker compose up -d
```

Check the service health with:

```sh
docker compose ps
```
