## OAuth2 and OIDC login

Social login uses Authlib with Google (OIDC discovery) and GitHub. Register the
callback URL `OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE_URL/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback` with each
provider, then set the matching client id and secret.

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/auth/oauth/{provider}/login` | Redirect to Google or GitHub. |
| `GET` | `/auth/oauth/{provider}/callback` | Exchange the provider callback for a bearer token. |

Supported providers are `google` and `github`; any other value is rejected by
request validation. A missing or invalid callback `state` returns `403`. OAuth
identity is stored by provider subject and a verified email. An unverified or
missing email, subject, or provider id returns `400`. If the verified email
already belongs to a password account, the callback returns `409` and does not
link automatically; sign in with the local password instead. A new OAuth account
gets an unusable random password, so social-only accounts cannot use the password
login form until a password is set separately.

```sh
curl -L "http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/oauth/google/login"
```

Configure `OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE_URL` (default `http://localhost:8000`),
`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID`, and
`GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET`. The application stores OAuth state in a signed session
cookie using `SECRET_KEY`, so keep that value stable across restarts.
