## MongoDB and Beanie

Beanie initializes from the `MONGODB_URL` and `MONGODB_DB` settings during the
application lifespan. The defaults connect to a local MongoDB instance:

```text
mongodb://localhost:27017
app
```

The `documents` collection stores `name`, `description`, and `created_at` fields.
The CRUD endpoints reuse the same bounded pagination contract as the relational
example:

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/documents` | Create a document and return it with status `201`. |
| `GET` | `/documents` | List documents ordered by id with `limit` and `offset`. |
| `GET` | `/documents/{document_id}` | Return one document or `404`. |
| `PATCH` | `/documents/{document_id}` | Update the provided fields or return `404`. |
| `DELETE` | `/documents/{document_id}` | Delete one document and return `204`, or `404`. |

```sh
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/documents" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name": "first", "description": "example"}'

curl "http://127.0.0.1:8000/documents?limit=20&offset=0"
```

The tests use `mongomock-motor`, so they do not need a live MongoDB server.
