## Cache helpers

`{{ spec.package }}.core.cache_helpers` provides a namespaced `Cache` class and
a `cache_aside` decorator. The decorator serializes results as JSON, reuses them
on later calls, and accepts a per-function TTL:

```python
from {{ spec.package }}.core.cache_helpers import cache_aside, create_cache

cache = create_cache(namespace="example", default_ttl=60)


@cache_aside(cache, lambda item_id: f"item:{item_id}", ttl=30)
async def load_item(item_id: int) -> dict[str, int]:
    return {"id": item_id}
```

`Cache` accepts any backend that implements the `CacheBackend` protocol, so
tests can use an in-memory fake without a running Redis server.
{% endif %}
