## Authentication abuse protection

JWT projects always install an in-process throttle at
`app.state.auth_throttle`, even when the optional `rate-limit` feature is not
selected. It keys on the client address and the route scope. Registration and
email requests allow 5 per minute; login, logout, reset, and verification allow
10; OAuth login and callback allow 20; `/auth/me` allows 60. Exceeding a limit
returns `429` with `Retry-After`. The throttle is per process; put a shared
limiter at the proxy for multi-worker deployments.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("rate-limit") %}

## Rate limiting

The optional SlowAPI feature installs a limiter as `app.state.limiter` with a
default limit of 100 requests per minute and adds the `/limited` example route.
Authentication routes use the mandatory throttle described above instead.
Exceeding a limit returns `429` with a JSON `detail` field.
{% endif %}
