## File uploads

Uploads are stored through the `Storage` protocol in
`{{ spec.package }}.core.storage`. The default `LocalStorage` backend writes to
`UPLOAD_DIR` (`uploads` by default) and creates missing parent directories. All
routes require a bearer token, and generated keys are prefixed with the owner's
user id; another user's key returns `404`.

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/uploads` | Store a file after checking its type and size and return `201` with a generated `key`. |
| `GET` | `/uploads/{key}` | Download a stored file owned by the caller or return `404`. |
| `DELETE` | `/uploads/{key}` | Delete a stored file owned by the caller and return `204`. |

`MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES` defaults to `5000000`. `ALLOWED_UPLOAD_TYPES` lists the
accepted media types and defaults to PNG, JPEG, PDF, and plain text. PNG, JPEG,
and PDF content must match its magic bytes; plain text must be valid UTF-8.
Mismatched content returns `415`; oversized files return `413`. Stored keys are generated on
the server and resolved below the configured directory, so path traversal
attempts are rejected.

```sh
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
  -F "file=@example.png;type=image/png"

curl "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads/<key>" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"

curl -X DELETE "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads/<key>" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```
{% endif %}
